<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.healthkit</key>
	<true/>
	<!--
	  Push notifications need this, with the value "development" or
	  "production":

	    aps-environment

	  Left out for the same reason as the two below: a free personal team's
	  profile cannot carry it, and signing fails if it is here. Registration
	  in Push.swift fails harmlessly until then. Enable Push Notifications on
	  the app id in the developer portal once enrolled, add the key here, and
	  set APNS_KEY_ID, APNS_TEAM_ID and APNS_P8 on the Convex deployment.
	-->
	<!--
	  Signing in with Apple's own sheet needs this:

	    com.apple.developer.applesignin  (an array holding the string "Default")

	  Left out for the same reason as the others here: a free personal team's
	  profile cannot carry it. Until then the app uses Apple's web sign-in when
	  the deployment has AUTH_APPLE_ID and AUTH_APPLE_SECRET. Once enrolled,
	  enable Sign in with Apple on the app id, add the key here, and set
	  AppConfig.appleSignInSheet to true.
	-->
	<!--
	  Running a downloaded 4B model needs these two:

	    com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit
	    com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing

	  A 4B model at 4-bit is ~2.6GB of weights plus a KV cache, which the
	  default per-app ceiling kills long before it finishes loading. They are
	  commented out because a free personal team's provisioning profile cannot
	  carry them — signing fails with "doesn't include the Increased Memory
	  Limit capability". Enable both in the developer portal once the account
	  is enrolled in the paid program, then restore them here.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
